{% doc %}
  One product-quiz result: the reused horizontal product card with an icon-only quick-add button
  (single-variant products add directly, multi-variant ones open the quick-view modal).

  Shared by the data endpoint (sections/section-rendering-product-quiz.liquid) and the theme-editor
  preview rows of blocks/_product-quiz-results.liquid, so both render the exact same row. The
  endpoint cannot read the results block's settings, so vendor and title clamp are rendered
  permissively here and narrowed by the results list in CSS (`--line-clamp`, the no-vendor
  modifier) — see src/scss/scoped/product-quiz.scss.

  Every row is a BOX card. The endpoint passes no scheme, so its cards come out with the theme's
  `pcard_box_color_scheme`, which the runtime swaps for the results list's `data-row-scheme`; the
  editor preview rows pass the results block's scheme directly.

  @param {object} [product] - The product. Blank renders the onboarding placeholder card (shop name as its vendor).
  @param {string} [color_scheme] - Colour scheme id painting the box panel (default: the theme's box card scheme).

  @example
  {% render 'product-quiz-row', product: product, color_scheme: row_color_scheme %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- capture card -%}
  {%- render 'product-card-markup',
    product: product,
    view_event_context: 'recommendation',
    mode: 'horizontal',
    mode_mobile: 'horizontal',
    style: 'box',
    color_scheme: color_scheme,
    image_ratio: '1',
    media_width: '9rem',
    media_width_mobile: '7rem',
    show_badges: false,
    show_badges_mobile: false,
    show_swatch: false,
    show_swatch_mobile: false,
    show_quick_view: false,
    show_quick_view_mobile: false,
    show_quick_add: true,
    show_quick_add_mobile: true,
    quick_add_button_layout: 'icon-only',
    quick_add_placement: 'actions',
    show_vendor: true,
    show_vendor_mobile: true,
    show_type: false,
    show_type_mobile: false,
    product_title_line_limit: 'none',
    form_id_suffix: 'quiz'
  -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- liquid
  comment
    Onboarding card (no product): the core placeholder has no vendor line and no title clamp
    class, so `show_vendor` and `title_line_limit` would show nothing in the editor preview.
    Give it the shop name as its vendor (hidden by the list's no-vendor modifier like a real
    one) and a `text-limit-*` title, which reads the list's `--line-clamp`.
  endcomment
  if product == blank
    capture placeholder_title
      echo '<div class="product-card__metas pointer-pass-through"><span class="product-card__meta product-card__meta--vendor"><span class="reversed-link__text">'
      echo shop.name | escape
      echo '</span></span></div><p class="product-card__title text-wrap text-limit-none">'
    endcapture
    assign card = card | replace_first: '<p class="product-card__title text-wrap">', placeholder_title
  endif
-%}
<div class="product-quiz-results__product" data-quiz-product-id="{{ product.id }}">
  {{- card -}}
</div>
